                    <div class="featured-card-glow"></div>
                    <div class="featured-card-content">
                        <div class="featured-card-icon">♾️</div>
                        <div class="featured-card-text">
                            <div class="featured-badge">编辑精选 · 第 1 本</div>
                            <h4 class="featured-card-title">《有限与无限的游戏》</h4>
                            <p class="featured-card-author">詹姆斯·卡斯 · 1987</p>
                            <p class="featured-card-desc">詹姆斯·卡斯在 1987 年提出的革命性框架,深刻揭示了人类社会始终存在的两种根本不同的游戏模式:有限游戏在边界内玩,目的是赢得胜利;无限游戏玩边界本身,目的是让游戏继续。本书被誉为重新理解商业、教育、婚姻与人生哲学的奠基之作,深刻影响了乔布斯等众多领袖的思维方式。</p>
                        </div>
                        <span class="featured-card-cta">
                            阅读 <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-long"></i>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </a>

                <a href="7-ge-xi-guan.html" class="featured-card cube-card" data-num="02">
                    <div class="featured-card-num">02</div>
                    <div class="featured-card-glow"></div>
                    <div class="featured-card-content">
                        <div class="featured-card-icon">🎯</div>
                        <div class="featured-card-text">
                            <div class="featured-badge">编辑精选 · 第 2 本</div>
                            <h4 class="featured-card-title">《7个习惯》</h4>
                            <p class="featured-card-author">史蒂芬·柯维 · 1989</p>
                            <p class="featured-card-desc">史蒂芬·柯维被《时代周刊》评为"美国最有影响力的 25 人之一"。本书提出的"积极主动、以终为始、要事第一、双赢思维、知彼解己、统合综效、不断更新"七大习惯,塑造了现代个人管理学的基石。全球数亿人将其视为人生指南,被译为 40 多种语言持续畅销 30 余年。</p>
                        </div>
                        <span class="featured-card-cta">
                            阅读 <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-long"></i>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </a>

                <a href="siqian-ge-xingqi.html" class="featured-card cube-card" data-num="03">
                    <div class="featured-card-num">03</div>
                    <div class="featured-card-glow"></div>
                    <div class="featured-card-content">
                        <div class="featured-card-icon">⏳</div>
                        <div class="featured-card-text">
                            <div class="featured-badge">编辑精选 · 第 3 本</div>
                            <h4 class="featured-card-title">《4000周》</h4>
                            <p class="featured-card-author">Oliver Burkeman · 2022</p>
                            <p class="featured-card-desc">假如一个人能活到 75 岁,大约有 4000 周。英国作家 Oliver Burkeman 用哲学的深邃与英式幽默告诉我们:时间管理的真正秘诀不是挤出更多时间,而是接受我们的有限。本书颠覆了所有效率主义鸡汤,在 2022 年成为全球现象级畅销书,被誉为这个焦虑时代的"清醒剂"。</p>
                        </div>
                        <span class="featured-card-cta">
                            阅读 <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-long"></i>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </a>

                <a href="moli-sikao-dafa.html" class="featured-card cube-card" data-num="04">
                    <div class="featured-card-num">04</div>
                    <div class="featured-card-glow"></div>
                    <div class="featured-card-content">
                        <div class="featured-card-icon">✨</div>
                        <div class="featured-card-text">
                            <div class="featured-badge">编辑精选 · 第 4 本</div>
                            <h4 class="featured-card-title">《魔力思考大法》</h4>
                            <p class="featured-card-author">大卫·施瓦茨 · 1959</p>
                            <p class="featured-card-desc">大卫·施瓦茨的经典之作,被誉为"思考的圣经"。本书深刻揭示:思考的质量决定人生的高度。成功者与失败者的区别,不在于机遇或天赋,而在于他们如何思考问题。本书自 1959 年出版以来,持续激励了数代人去相信思考的力量,被许多商业领袖列为必读经典。</p>
                        </div>
                        <span class="featured-card-cta">
                            阅读 <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-long"></i>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </a>

                <a href="biran.html" class="featured-card cube-card" data-num="05">
